WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.220
The gloriously colourful and glitter-filled
world of Trolls gets a whole lot bigger in

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:09.710
Trolls World Tour when Poppy and Branch discover
there are six Troll tribes, including the

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:12.850
fearsome Rock Trolls led by hard-rocker Queen
Barb!

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:17.880
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing over 50 amazing hidden

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.230
details, easter eggs, and secrets packed into
the brand new Trolls sequel.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:26.920
And keep watching to learn how you can win
one of these incredible official movie merch

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:27.920
packs.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:32.640
When Queen Barb and her Hard Rock crew gate-crash
the Techno Trolls' underwater rave, they arrive

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.010
in some scary-looking critters called Angler
Buses.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:41.170
The design of the Angler Bus is based on the
real-life anglerfish, an ambush predator often

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:45.680
found in the murky depths of the sea, up to
a mile below the surface.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.530
Using that particular fish as inspiration
for the Rock Trolls' transport was a great

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:53.640
choice by the filmmakers,
because anglerfish are usually dark and have

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:58.609
loads of sharp teeth in their enormous mouths
which can expand to swallow prey up to twice

00:00:58.609 --> 00:01:03.200
as big as their bodies;
and all of that perfectly fits the Hard Rock

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:08.750
Trolls' terrifying vibe as well as their punk-rock
style with all its dark leather, denim, and

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.050
metal spikes and studs.

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:15.300
During Barb's "Crazy Train" song, we see the
angler buses burst out of the ocean and drive

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:18.020
around madly on land while she rocks out.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:22.570
World Tour director Walt Dohrn has said this
scene was inspired by the huge chase sequence

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:27.180
from Mad Max: Fury Road which included crazy
drummers and rock guitarists playing on some

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:31.030
insane and gargantuan vehicles while speeding
across the land.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:35.770
Just like the first film, the animation in
Trolls World Tour is astounding and there's

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:40.750
such an incredibly tactile, textured quality
to both movies that you feel you could almost

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:44.240
reach out and touch it in all its felty, fuzziness.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:48.220
And right from the start, there's loads of
lovely little visual details.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:53.040
The underwater empire of the Techno Trolls
mixes the digital world of techno with the

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.810
home-made textiles we see in many of the other
troll lands.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:01.780
Which means we not only get lasers, LEDs,
and trolls with fibre-optic hair, glow-paint

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:06.640
patterned skin, and 8-bit beating hearts,
but we also get landscapes made of crochet

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:10.660
and macramé, that's the art of making things
using knots.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:15.280
And the way the neon-coloured crowd moves,
at first draws on the natural world, mimicking

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:19.030
the motion of a wave in the sea, which is
a nice touch given they live underwater;

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:23.920
but as the song's about to reach its peak,
things look more digital and the way they

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:28.440
move takes on the look of a spectrum analyser
on a home stereo.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:32.900
When it comes to the film's title, if you
look closely at the fiery flames beneath it,

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:36.420
you'll see that they look like bright orange
strands of Troll hair!

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:41.810
As for the waterfall in the Pop Troll kingdom,
that's made of long, narrow strips of shiny

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:43.069
tinsel!

00:02:43.069 --> 00:02:47.330
And the lonesome, dusty world of the Country
Trolls is filled with buildings shaped like

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:52.870
patchwork-quilted cacti, roads made of burlap,
and when you see the farmland from above,

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:56.590
it looks like an enormous multi-coloured patchwork
quilt.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:03:00.200
The filmmakers wanted to make the big chase
scene where Hickory and the Pop Trolls are

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:04.620
run out of town feel like how kids play with
their Troll toys at home on their bedspreads,

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:10.940
so they decided to make the cliff they fall
down out of a stack of quilts and folded blankets.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:14.970
And did you notice how crucial vinyl records
are in the design of the Funk Trolls' home?

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:19.480
Not only is the room where they keep their
tribe's musical string full of columns made

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:24.720
out of records, but the outside of their spaceship
is mostly made out of silver records.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:29.280
Also, instead of the scrapbooks that tell
the Pop Trolls' pop-washed version of Troll

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:34.630
history, when Prince D tells Poppy the real
history of the six tribes, visually the story's

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:38.160
told using the cover art of a double album.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.800
The little gem that the Classical Trolls have
on their tummies is a lovely tribute to the

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.580
1990s toys called Treasure Trolls that had
a little jewel in their belly button which

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:47.690
you could make a wish on.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:51.921
And in fact, there was already a reference
to those particular troll toys in the Trolls

00:03:51.921 --> 00:03:53.130
Holiday Special.

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:54.620
♪ Good Luck Troll Day
Put a gem on your stomach ♪

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:56.230
♪ Then you spread a little charm
Let a friend belly rub it ♪

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:58.540
♪ Rub it, rub it, rub it
Rub it, rub it, rub it ♪

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:02.330
The leader of the Classical Trolls is called
Trollzart, which is a play on the name of

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:07.819
the famous classical music composer Mozart,
who like his World Tour counterpart was also

00:04:07.819 --> 00:04:10.060
often pictured wearing a white wig.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:15.110
Keeping with the classical theme of Symphonyville,
if you listen very closely, you can hear the

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:20.239
tribe's critters all bleating the word 'Baaach',
which is a pun on the name of the renowned

00:04:20.239 --> 00:04:25.870
classical music composer, Bach, mixed with
the usual baa sound made by sheep or goats.

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:26.870
"Baaah..."

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:27.870
"Baaach."

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:31.460
Oh, and if you look closely at the animals'
design too, you'll see that their legs even

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:33.680
look like little musical notes!

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:38.550
World Tour also has many call-backs and similarities
to the first Trolls movie.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:40.210
"Oh, I can stop the feeling."

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:44.860
Barb and the Hard Rock Trolls invade the Techno
Troll kingdom just as they're in the middle

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:49.689
of a huge rave party, similar to the first
movie and how the Bergen Chef found the trolls

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:52.719
in the forest when Poppy threw a big party.

00:04:52.719 --> 00:04:57.389
And when Cooper poops out a three-tier cake
with candles after he's terrified by some

00:04:57.389 --> 00:04:59.430
weird and wonderful creatures,
"Happy Birthday?"

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:04.770
it's a call-back to how he was so scared that
he pooped out cupcakes when Chef invaded the

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:07.190
Troll kingdom in the first film.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:08.190
"Erm...

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:09.190
Cupcake?"

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:12.849
And if you keep watching through the movie's
credits, you'll see those strange creatures

00:05:12.849 --> 00:05:15.069
gobble up Cooper's cake!

00:05:15.069 --> 00:05:18.919
Also in the credits is a Caterbus similar
to the one from Trolls Holiday.

00:05:18.919 --> 00:05:23.499
And like so much of the "strange fairytale-like
dream" quality of the Trolls franchise, the

00:05:23.499 --> 00:05:28.159
various weird critters the Trolls use for
transport owe a great deal to the odd creatures

00:05:28.159 --> 00:05:33.370
and dream-like worlds created by renowned
Japanese writer-director Hayao Miyazaki, who

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:38.410
co-founded Studio Ghibli and gave us such
classic animated movies as My Neighbour Totorro,

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:40.889
which featured the iconic Cat-bus.

00:05:40.889 --> 00:05:43.620
OK spoilers ahead for the ending of the movie
now.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:47.199
You can skip to the time on screen to avoid
them if you prefer.

00:05:47.199 --> 00:05:51.169
Another call-back in World Tour is when the
six strings are destroyed and all the trolls

00:05:51.169 --> 00:05:53.960
lose their colour,
similar to how the trolls faded to grey in

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:57.110
the original movie when they were trapped
and thought they were all about to be eaten

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:58.110
by the Bergens.

00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:03.930
In the sequel, the trolls' colour begins to
return when Cooper notices his own heartbeat

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.220
and that the music is still inside him.

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:11.759
We see his heart glow and slowly, bit by bit,
each of the other trolls' hearts also lights

00:06:11.759 --> 00:06:14.869
up as they sing and their colour returns to
them.

00:06:14.869 --> 00:06:18.979
The fact that music is in the Trolls' hearts
and not the strings was hinted at several

00:06:18.979 --> 00:06:22.900
times earlier with many heart patterns and
symbols appearing throughout the movie,

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:27.360
from the thumping heart beat in the opening
scene,

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:30.180
to heart symbols on the chests of the Techno
Trolls,

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:33.889
the heart-shaped bubbles they blow,
and the explosion of digital hearts when King

00:06:33.889 --> 00:06:37.539
Trollex drops the beat;
to the Pop Trolls' heart formation during

00:06:37.539 --> 00:06:39.110
their opening medley.

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:44.099
Then there's the heart shape the Classical
Trolls and the Country Trolls form when playing;

00:06:44.099 --> 00:06:48.160
the heart-shaped glasses that Poppy, Branch
and Biggie wear when they perform in Lonesome

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:51.099
Flats;
Chaz's heart-shaped chest-hair and the heart

00:06:51.099 --> 00:06:54.210
pattern he blows with the petals from his
saxophone;

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:59.039
"I can't feel my face."
and when the Funk Trolls sing "It's All Love",

00:06:59.039 --> 00:07:03.430
some of the spinning records light up and
pulse in a heart-shaped pattern.

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:07.219
If you enjoyed watching the Bergens in the
first movie and the Holiday short, then you'll

00:07:07.219 --> 00:07:11.050
be glad that, even though they don't have
a starring role this time, they at least get

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:13.050
a little cameo in the new film.

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:17.339
After Poppy and Branch fly off together during
the movie's credits, Queen Bridget and King

00:07:17.339 --> 00:07:21.439
Gristle pop up in a quick mid-credits scene
where we find out that they're disappointed

00:07:21.439 --> 00:07:22.870
to have missed out on all the fun.

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:26.509
"Aw, Grissy, I guess we're late to the party."

00:07:26.509 --> 00:07:27.970
"Aw, balls!"

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:28.970
"Grissy."

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:30.930
"But who's gonna eat my cheese balls, babe?"

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:36.089
As well as the many other Troll tribes, we
get to meet some brand new Pop Trolls including

00:07:36.089 --> 00:07:41.249
Legsly, who has extendable legs meaning she
can go from short to tall very quickly.

00:07:41.249 --> 00:07:45.180
Unlike the other trolls though she can't extend
and manipulate her hair, and there's a nod

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:49.650
to this when the Pop Trolls use their hair
as legs to dance about during their opening

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:50.650
song.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:55.119
Oh, and by the way, Legsly, which definitely
feels like a limb-based pun on the name Lesley,

00:07:55.119 --> 00:07:58.629
is voiced by the aca-awesome singer-songwriter
Ester Dean.

00:07:58.629 --> 00:07:59.629
"Thanks, Poppy.

00:07:59.629 --> 00:08:01.249
Kisses and donuts and sprinkles!"

00:08:01.249 --> 00:08:05.620
Who's not only written masses of hits for
the likes of Rihanna and Katy Perry, but she

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:10.840
also played Barden Bella Cynthia-Rose in the
Pitch Perfect movies alongside Poppy voice

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:12.490
actress Anna Kendrick.

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:18.191
Another new Pop Troll is Skyscraper who, like
Legsly, is also the opposite of many of the

00:08:18.191 --> 00:08:22.810
other Pop Trolls because he's a fuzzling-style
troll who has an enormous body of hair all

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:24.229
the way down to his feet.

00:08:24.229 --> 00:08:29.789
But unlike fellow fuzzlings such as Fuzzbert
who have no head or face, Skyscraper has four

00:08:29.789 --> 00:08:31.740
heads all of which speak in unison.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:32.740
"Or Skyscraper Troll?"

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:33.889
"Yeah, different like me?"

00:08:33.889 --> 00:08:38.349
And Skyscraper was voiced by the podcasting
McElroy Brothers who campaigned to appear

00:08:38.349 --> 00:08:43.330
in World Tour after they discovered YouTubers
had voiced characters in the first movie.

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:48.290
Each brother also voiced additional characters,
with Justin playing the parts of Beat Drop

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:51.350
Button
"Let's do this, King Trollex!"

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:53.509
And Tumbleweed;
"You suck!"

00:08:53.509 --> 00:08:58.310
And Griffin voicing Country Music Tear while
Travis did Rocker Tear.

00:08:58.310 --> 00:09:03.319
When the Snack Pack goes undercover to infiltrate
the Rock Trolls, they each wear outfits and

00:09:03.319 --> 00:09:05.930
designs referencing icons from Rock 'n' Roll.

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:07.680
"We need to go undercover."

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:08.680
"But how?"

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:09.680
"With fashion!"

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:13.250
Biggie and Dinkles each take on a different
look from Elvis Presley.

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:17.870
Legsly has a black-and-white striped outfit
that references Elvis's Jailhouse Rock.

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:22.220
And Satin and Chenille's clothes and red and
white pompoms are nods to the cheerleaders

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:24.140
in the musical movie Grease.

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:26.220
"One, two, three, four!"

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:28.830
♪ Rainbows, unicorns
♪ Everything nice, yeah

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:31.960
♪ Sugarplums, fairy dust
♪ Everything nice, yeah

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.520
♪ Brush your teeth.

